# Gates the CI test job runs after it installs pytest (tests/requirements-pytest.txt) into .venv-tests and
# writes the pull request's title and body into pr-inputs/ (.github/workflows/ci.yml).
# Mutation, only dashboard/: the gate modules are tested by running them as scripts, and mutmut sees only the
# code a test runs in its own process.
changed-code-mutation --source dashboard/**/*.py --python .venv-tests/bin/python
# Both run the suite the way the job's own test step does: python3 and unittest.
# A report-only pilot (--soak): it prints findings as warnings and never fails the job, but a run that cannot be
# judged (exit 2) still does.
regression-test-fails-on-base --soak --title pr-inputs/title.txt --body pr-inputs/body.md
# coverage-not-lost blocks: it soaked from #214, and the 22 pull requests in a row checked before promoting it
# (#302 to #323) had no false alarm and no run it could not judge. It runs on the dashboard tests only: on the whole
# suite, whose tests run each gate as a child process that coverage.py measures too, a pull request takes about an
# hour (four runs of 784 to 1030 seconds, PR #220), so the whole suite runs once a night instead, report-only
# (.github/workflows/nightly.yml).
coverage-not-lost --runner unittest --args "discover -s tests -p 'test_dashboard_*.py'" --body pr-inputs/body.md --timeout 300
